@Jonathansmith5050 Hi, thank you so much for your kind words!
What you see on my profile are actually Corinthian capitals from the Roman period, which I managed to recreate in 3D thanks to the platform Meshy.ai.
The references for the drawings come from Luigi Canina’s "Gli edifizj di Roma antica" (1848–1851) and George Ledwell Taylor’s "The Architectural Antiquities of Rome" (1821). From these works I found the original capital drawings that I used for my 3D reconstructions!

